Here are 3-5 specific, actionable recommendations for the Avoid Logging Sensitive Data gate:

1. Implement logging suppression for sensitive data in the `application.properties` file by adding the following configuration:
```
logging:
  level:
    com.example.sensitive.data: WARN
    com.example.another.sensitive.data: INFO
```
This will suppress logging of sensitive data at the WARN and INFO levels, reducing the risk of exposing sensitive information. Review the codebase to identify potential sources of sensitive data that should be suppressed.

2. Modify the `SensitiveDataHandler` class in `com.example.util` to use a custom logging filter instead of the default logger. For example:
```
public class SensitiveDataHandler {
    private final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SensitiveDataHandler.class);

    public void handle(String data) {
        if (isSensitive(data)) {
            // Use a custom logging filter to suppress sensitive data
            logger.filter(new CustomLoggingFilter());
        } else {
            logger.info(data);
        }
    }
}
```
This will ensure that sensitive data is not logged at all, reducing the risk of exposure. Implement the `CustomLoggingFilter` class to implement the necessary logic for suppressing sensitive data.

